# Normalize line endings to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# CI runs on Linux; development happens on Windows and elsewhere. A Windows
# checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` (git's default there) writes CRLF into the
# working tree, so any tool that inspects line endings disagrees with CI:
#
#   - `npm run format:check` reported 1167 files — effectively the whole repo —
#     because Prettier's `endOfLine` default is "lf". Real drift was invisible
#     in that noise, and CI's 6 genuine hits went unnoticed across two merges.
#   - `docs/api/openapi.v1.json` is byte-compared by
#     `scripts/snapshot-openapi.ts --check`, which is why it already carried
#     this rule individually. The rule below generalizes it.
#
# `eol=lf` is what does the work: `text=auto` on its own still lets
# core.autocrlf convert on checkout. With this in place the working tree is
# byte-identical across platforms, so every tool — Prettier, ESLint, the
# OpenAPI byte compare, shell scripts, Docker builds — sees what CI sees.
#
# Deliberately NOT paired with Prettier's `endOfLine: "auto"`. That would also
# make the check pass on Windows, but only by tolerating mixed endings, and
# only for Prettier. This fixes the cause rather than one symptom.
#
# One-time refresh for existing clones after this lands — see the
# Windows-Specific Notes section of CLAUDE.md:
#
#   git rm --cached -r . && git reset --hard
#
* text=auto eol=lf

# Drizzle migration snapshots are generated, load-bearing, and enormous. Each
# is drizzle-kit's diff base — the full schema serialized to JSON, ~12k lines
# apiece — and CI's offline drift gate regenerates against the latest one,
# so they must stay committed byte-for-byte. But they drown review: one
# 21-line schema change, carrying 2 lines of migration SQL, once diffed at
# +24,315 lines with the regenerated snapshots along for the ride.
#
# `linguist-generated` makes GitHub collapse these files in PR diffs and drop
# them from language stats. Rendering only — storage, merges, and local diffs
# are untouched. Deliberately NOT `-diff` (git would treat them as binary,
# hiding content exactly when a concurrent-migration conflict needs a hand
# re-mint) and deliberately not the .sql files: the SQL is the upgrade path
# for released installs, and is precisely what review must see.
apps/*/drizzle/meta/*.json linguist-generated=true
